/// Retained node tree and layout for `.j3ui` components. Styles come from `j3.ui.css`; this
/// module produces rectangles and text fragments, it paints nothing. Main thread only.
/// Generated `.j3ui` code drives this; most programs only touch `Dom` for `setFrameMs`, `simInput`, and
/// `dumpHtml` (`j3c doc testing`). The markup is `j3c doc j3ui`, the CSS is `j3c doc css`.
///
/// ```
/// let css = Css.new(&mem);  parse(&css, theme, "ui/theme.css", 0);
/// let d = Dom.new(&mem, &css);
/// // every frame (cheap when nothing changed):
/// d.begin();
/// let box = d.open(0, d.tag("div"), 1);  d.cls(box, "card");
///     d.text("Hello");
/// d.close();
/// d.end();
/// d.layoutAt(1280.0, 760.0);              // no work when nothing changed
/// let w = d.nodes.items[box].w;         // rects: x, y relative to the parent's border box
/// ```
///
/// Build API: `begin`, `open(slot, tag, scope): id` (reuses the child at that position when slot,
/// tag and scope match; slots increase within a parent, a stale earlier sibling is dropped),
/// `text(s)`, `close`, `end` (unvisited children of the last frame are removed and their ids go
/// to a free list). `cls`/`clsIf`, `attrType`, `attrDisabled`, `attrChecked`, `attrValue`,
/// `attrMin`/`attrMax`/`attrStep`, `setFlag` (hover/active) mark the style dirty only on a real
/// change. `{#each}` / `{#if}` need no support: use distinct slots per branch and iteration.
///
/// Units are CSS px (logical); multiply by the UI scale when painting. Results, per node:
/// `x`, `y` (relative to the parent's border box; inline elements sit at 0,0 and text fragments
/// are relative to the block that owns them), `w`, `h` (border box), `scrollY`, `scrollMax`,
/// `contentH` (scroll height of an `overflow-y: auto` box), `baseline`. Text is in fragments:
/// walk `frag0` then `Frag.next` of the owner block (a block that has inline children, or a text
/// node that is itself a flex/grid item); each `Frag` is a run of one text node (`start..end` bytes
/// of `textOf(node)`) with `x`, `y` (top of the font line box, where `drawText` takes its position)
/// and `w`. Fragments with `kind == 1` are inline-blocks (read the node's own rect instead).
/// Decorated inline elements (padding, border, background) have one rect per line in `box0` then `Dom.boxes[..].next`
/// of the same owner (`Frag` with `kind 2`: `node` the element, `x`/`y`/`w`, `ap` the height, `start`/`end` 1 on the first/last piece).
/// `absX`/`absY` walk the parents (scroll offsets included).
///
/// Layout subset (what idle-breakout uses, checked against the numbers Chrome gives):
/// - Block flow: children stack and stretch. NO margin collapsing (`ponytail:` margins add).
/// - Inline: text and `span`/`small` (and inline-blocks such as a lone `button`) wrap into line boxes
///   at the box width; `text-align`, `line-height`, white-space collapsing. An inline element has
///   no box of its own (no padding or background on a `span`). `white-space: nowrap | pre-line | pre | pre-wrap`,
///   `overflow-wrap: break-word` (a word wider than the line is cut between code points), and
///   `text-overflow: ellipsis` (with `overflow-y` not visible: the first run past the edge is cut and
///   ends in a "…", `Frag.ell`). `justify` stretches soft-wrapped interword gaps; `line-clamp` limits the block's inline content (text and spans) to N lines. No `word-break`.
/// - Flex: row/column and their reverse directions, numeric grow (`flex`), `flex-basis`, weighted `flex-shrink`, min/max redistribution,
///   `gap`/`row-gap`, `justify-content` (start end center space-between around evenly),
///   `align-items` (stretch start end center baseline), `min-width`/`min-height` including the
///   `auto` rule (min-content; 0 for a scroll container). `flex-wrap: wrap | wrap-reverse` with a definite main size
///   breaks it into lines (`layoutFlex`; physical row/column gaps, `align-content` places lines). `align-self` overrides
///   cross alignment; stable integer `order` changes visual/hit order only. Reverse directions change geometry only.
/// - Grid: `repeat(n, 1fr)`, `1fr auto`, px tracks, auto rows, `gap`/`row-gap`, items in source order.
/// - Absolute: against the nearest `position: relative`/`absolute` ancestor or the root;
///   `left right top bottom inset`, shrink-to-fit width. The static position is the parent's content origin.
/// - `overflow-x` / `overflow-y` / `overflow`: `scrollMax` / `scrollMaxX` from the content size; `auto` and `scroll` take the wheel
///   (`wheelRoute`: innermost box that can move, chaining outward, `overscroll-behavior`, inertia with `scroll-behavior: smooth`)
///   and draw scrollbars (`barsOf`, `j3.ui.scrollbar`); children far outside a clip box neither paint nor take the mouse.
/// - `position: fixed`, `<dialog>` and overlays (`attrOverlay`, `Dom.ovs`): viewport coordinates, painted without the ancestors' clips
///   (`paint.pushNoClip`), found through the entries of their stacking context (`hitEntry`); `left`/`top` attributes, `position-try-fallbacks`, keep-inside clamp.
/// - `box-sizing`, `padding`, `margin` (`auto` gives the box the free space: centered in a block with a width, on either flex axis, between `left`/`right` or `top`/`bottom` of an absolute box; elsewhere 0), `aspect-ratio`, `outline`, `border` widths, `width`/`height`/
///   `min-*` in px, % and `calc()`/`min()`/`max()`/`clamp()`/viewport units (`lenVal`, `j3.ui.csscalc`), `height: 100%` of a definite parent (a stretched flex item is definite).
/// - Replaced boxes: `input[type=checkbox]` and `input[type=radio]` 16x16, `input[type=range]` 129x16, `input[type=color]` 44x24, other inputs and `select` 160x28, `textarea` 200 x (`rows`, default 3) lines.
///   `<option>` is `display: none` (a `select` reads its options; `j3c doc j3ui`).
///
/// Fonts: the `@font-face` that matches `font-family` (else the first one) gives the ttf path,
/// loaded lazily per (family, size); bold (weight 600+) uses `TTF_STYLE_BOLD`. Text is measured
/// with `j3.game.textWidth` (SDL_ttf only, no window).
///
/// Incremental: a changed text or class marks the node and its ancestors dirty. `layout` skips a
/// subtree that is clean and gets the same width and height again; a steady frame runs no layout.
///
/// Runtime (stage 05; the generated-code contract is `speculative/12_ui_runtime/README.md`): `beginFrame(size)`,
/// `layout()`, `endFrame()` frame the build walk; input (`clicked`, `mouseDown/Up/Move`, `wheelAt`, `localMouse`,
/// `dragging`/`rangeValue`, `changed`/`strValue`/`value` and `attrText` for the input widgets (`j3.ui.inputs`), hover/active/disabled restyle, wheel scroll) comes from the mouse or `simInput`;
/// `enter`/`leave` offset slots; `trans` gives `transition:` / `in:` / `out:` (leaving keeps a ghost); `paintNext`/`paintBox`/
/// `paintEnd` and `beginCanvas`/`endCanvas` paint through `j3.gfx.paint` (backgrounds, borders, radii, opacity,
/// scale, clip, text, checkbox and range controls, transitions on background, border colors, color, opacity,
/// transform, nested stacking contexts for `z-index` and effects, `dom/stack.j3`). Text paints `text-shadow` and `-webkit-text-stroke`
/// through `j3.gfx.textfx` and a `background-clip: text` linear gradient through `paint.textGradient`. ponytail: hit testing follows `transform` but `localMouse` does not; one-sided borders are flat strips; a click on a label's text activates its control (`for="id"` or the first control inside; `j3.ui.inputs`); scene3d inside a canvas needs `gfx.setViewRect` with `absX/absY/size` by hand.
///
/// Untested in a real game (numbers, `stdlib/tests/dom_test.j3`, and `speculative/12_ui_runtime` only).

module j3.ui.dom;

